# WSLkit documentation baseline

Treat the **current** `README.md`, `docs/`, `docs/research/`, and `RFCs/` layout as the source of truth. Do not dump usage/params/flows/safety back into README. Do not treat `docs/design/` as Accepted decisions.

## Decision-document triad

| Location | Question |
|----------|----------|
| `RFCs/` | What should we do and why? |
| `docs/research/` | What have we learned / should we consider? |
| `docs/maintenance/reports/` | What did we actually do? |
| `docs/design/` | Pre-implementation working notes (excluded from routine user-doc governance unless asked) |

## README.md (product overview)

English section headings: Why WSLkit? / Features / Requirements / Quick Start / How It Works / Usage / Safety and Limitations / Documentation / License.

## docs/ (user-facing module docs)

```text
docs/
  portable.md         # Portable Model B (shipped; formerly usb.md)
  compact_vdisk.md
  install_wsl.md
  devkit.md
  design/
  research/
  maintenance/reports/
```

## Help language

All `Show-Help` / kit Help prints are **Chinese only**.

## Lifecycle (RFC-ARCH-001 Implemented)

- **Default:** Model B — export on media → host-local `wsl --import` → Eject re-export (optional skip) + unregister **host** copy.
- **Phase 2 (not shipped):** resident / `import-in-place`.
- Module name is **Portable** (not `Go`; `Usb` is a warning alias only).
- User docs and `kits/Portable.ps1` must stay aligned with Model B.
